"r+" as "open an existing file for both reading and writing.". "r+" = Read + Write, but the file must already exist.

Example
    Suppose test.txt already contains:
    "Hello Python"
    You can do:
    with open(r"C:\Users\...\test.txt", "r+") as file:
        data = file.read()
        print(data)
        file.write("I am learning Python.")